course: dictionary
lesson: 2216
title: One word, three jobs
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one the writer means. The word courier has three meanings: a person or company that delivers parcels, a guide who looks after tourists, and a verb meaning to send something by courier.
explain: «The parcel came by courier this morning.» The words parcel and came tell you a courier is a delivery person or company. Always ask: what word would fit here? If "delivery company" still makes sense in the sentence, you have found the right meaning.
explain: «The courier led our group around the old city and told us about every church.» Here a courier is a tour guide, because of the group, the city and the churches. Same word, different job. The context is the clue.
explain: «Plants cannot walk to each other, so they hire couriers and pay them in food.» The writer uses courier like a comparison: a bumblebee carries yellow pollen from one flower to the next, just as a delivery person carries a parcel from one place to another.
fact: A courier is a person or company that delivers parcels, letters or documents quickly to people's homes or businesses.
fact: A courier can also be someone who looks after a group of tourists on a trip.
fact: To courier something means to send it by courier, as in «We couriered the letter to the office.»
fact: In everyday life, a courier often brings online shopping in a van or on a bike.
fact: Safety: parcel scam messages often pretend to be from a courier, so check who is at the door before you open it.
exercise: «The parcel came by courier this morning.» What is a courier in this sentence? | A shop that sells parcels | *A delivery person or company | A tour guide with a flag | A type of bird
exercise: «The courier led our group around the old city and told us about every church.» What is the courier's job? | *To look after a group of tourists | To deliver a parcel to a house | To sell tickets at the station | To cook lunch for the group
exercise: Ella says, «Someone called and said they were a courier, so I should pay them now.» Why should Ella be careful? | Couriers always phone to ask for money | Couriers only send letters by post | *Parcel scam messages often pretend to be from a courier | Couriers never come to people's homes
test: «I couriered the contract to the office.» What does couriered mean here? | Lost on the way | Written by hand | *Sent by courier | Carried on a horse
test: «Plants hire couriers, and a bumblebee carries pollen from flower to flower.» What is the bumblebee like in this comparison? | A tourist on a trip | A parcel that is sent | *A delivery person, carrying something from place to place | A garden flower
exam: Which sentence uses courier as a verb? | *«We couriered the letter to Dad's office.» | «Our courier showed us the castle.» | «The courier wore a yellow jacket.» | «The courier van stopped outside our house.»
